1
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
The new morning we've finally found

2
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:08,150
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
is being hampered by the past.

4
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:12,190
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

5
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
What we chased after wasn't the future,

6
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:17,660
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
but the past so full of remorse.

8
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:21,490
Sugi bakari oikaketa

9
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

10
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:27,960
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

11
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

12
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:32,050
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

13
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
It's about now that a teardrop

14
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,890
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

15
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

16
00:00:37,890 --> 00:00:42,560
Kattou ga koboreochiru

17
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Will this rain ever stop?

18
00:00:42,890 --> 00:00:47,810
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

19
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
I've been freezing for a long time.

20
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:53,030
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

21
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

22
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:58,320
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

23
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
I wonder if it could embrace me.

24
00:00:58,320 --> 00:01:03,080
Tsutsumarete iikana

25
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Today, the rain falls again;

26
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:07,870
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

27
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

28
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:13,090
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

29
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

30
00:01:13,090 --> 00:01:18,130
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

31
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

32
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:29,850
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

33
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:34,900
Fullmetal!

34
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:38,990
He disappeared?!

35
00:01:39,610 --> 00:01:40,780
What did you do?!

36
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:53,840
He was simply escorted to a place
you'll eventually arrive at yourself.

37
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:03,600
What the hell is this?

38
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:07,390
This sensation...

39
00:02:08,390 --> 00:02:09,100
That's right!

40
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:12,980
The same sensation I got when I opened the Gate of Truth!

41
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:19,380
Sacrifices

42
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:19,380
Sacrifices

43
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,490
Dammit!

44
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:05,240
You son of a bitch!

45
00:03:26,390 --> 00:03:27,220
You're...!

46
00:03:27,970 --> 00:03:29,310
Idiot!

47
00:03:29,310 --> 00:03:30,600
Leave this place to us!

48
00:03:31,690 --> 00:03:34,730
It's our duty...

49
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:37,110
...to protect the young master.

50
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:43,280
It's impossible to carry this much weight with an automail!

51
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,320
Worry about your grandfather instead!

52
00:03:47,030 --> 00:03:47,870
It's...

53
00:03:48,830 --> 00:03:50,160
...too late.

54
00:03:54,370 --> 00:03:56,580
Briggs soldiers, lend me a hand!

55
00:03:58,340 --> 00:03:59,170
Right!

56
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:03,760
Bradley, eat this!

57
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:17,020
Fu!

58
00:04:19,570 --> 00:04:20,530
Fu!!

59
00:04:28,830 --> 00:04:30,450
Someone call a doctor!

60
00:04:30,450 --> 00:04:32,750
Are there any doctors well-versed in alchemy?!

61
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:33,910
I've...

62
00:04:33,910 --> 00:04:35,500
I've got a philosopher's stone right here!

63
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:38,130
Use as much of it as you need!

64
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,050
Anyone!

65
00:04:41,050 --> 00:04:42,260
Please!

66
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:45,180
Isn't Amestris the land of alchemy?!

67
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,300
There's gotta be someone here!

68
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:47,890
Hey!!

69
00:04:51,930 --> 00:04:53,140
Why...?

70
00:04:59,110 --> 00:04:59,900
Why...

71
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:05,610
Young master!

72
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:12,040
You monster...

73
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:17,920
Why...

74
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:24,960
I can't save a single vassal despite achieving immortality...?

75
00:05:25,970 --> 00:05:29,090
Fuck!!

76
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:32,260
Captain!

77
00:05:32,850 --> 00:05:35,020
Captain, get yourself together!

78
00:05:35,230 --> 00:05:36,480
Captain!

79
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:37,520
Captain!!

80
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:38,650
Captain!!

81
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:40,060
Fire!

82
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:53,540
We were able to give Bradley a fatal wound thanks to you.

83
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:58,370
Even though you ensured that Fu's death would not be in vain,

84
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:01,130
I can't even do a thing to help you.

85
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:11,590
Give me ammo!

86
00:06:11,590 --> 00:06:13,180
That was the last round!

87
00:06:16,350 --> 00:06:17,810
Shit!

88
00:06:17,810 --> 00:06:19,140
I'm out too!

89
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,310
Everyone, fire back with your rifles!

90
00:06:23,310 --> 00:06:24,230
Roger!

91
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:37,250
Lin Yao...

92
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:41,960
Or Greed, whichever you are...

93
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:47,460
If you're truly thankful, would you mind doing me a favor?

94
00:06:48,630 --> 00:06:55,470
We're not supposed to let this gate open until our Queen orders it to be.

95
00:06:57,100 --> 00:07:00,480
Please, protect it...

96
00:07:03,730 --> 00:07:07,530
It should be possible with your strength...

97
00:07:08,280 --> 00:07:13,030
No, only you... can do it...

98
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,410
I'm begging you...

99
00:07:39,470 --> 00:07:40,480
Greed.

100
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:42,190
Yo?

101
00:07:43,350 --> 00:07:44,770
I want power.

102
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:46,650
Lend me some.

103
00:07:49,190 --> 00:07:50,860
Sure thing.

104
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:53,780
We've still got some time until my next plan.

105
00:07:57,450 --> 00:08:00,160
Lan Fan, you protect the people here.

106
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,160
Roger!

107
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:05,580
Could you... do that for me?

108
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:08,090
Yeah, I promise.

109
00:08:11,630 --> 00:08:13,550
People from Xing...

110
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:19,010
...never break alliances!

111
00:08:23,850 --> 00:08:25,270
Fire! Fire!

112
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:40,790
W-Who the hell is that?!

113
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,450
All right, listen up!

114
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:46,830
Those who don't wish to get hurt,

115
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:49,790
and those who have family and lovers, stand back!

116
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:53,010
And women, too!

117
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:55,720
I don't particularly enjoy fighting women!

118
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:13,820
No way...!

119
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:14,880
Fire!!

120
00:10:36,070 --> 00:10:37,440
Incredible...

121
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:39,400
Lin Yao.

122
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:41,950
Or should I say, Homunculus?

123
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:58,970
How promising they are once you have one on your side...

124
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:01,510
Captain!

125
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:02,760
Captain!

126
00:11:09,850 --> 00:11:12,650
Captain, please hang in there!

127
00:11:12,650 --> 00:11:16,320
Did he... join our side?

128
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,110
Yes, sir!

129
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:21,570
Now I can kick the bucket in peace...

130
00:11:21,570 --> 00:11:23,610
What are you saying, Captain?!

131
00:11:23,610 --> 00:11:26,700
Major General Armstrong will achieve victory soon!

132
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,080
Just a little longer!

133
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:32,580
We need you to take an even more active role in Central than ever before!

134
00:11:38,710 --> 00:11:42,760
I don't like the sooty sky here in Central...

135
00:11:43,430 --> 00:11:46,220
Farewell, comrades...

136
00:11:47,350 --> 00:11:50,770
I'll go on ahead...

137
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:59,320
...to an even higher place than the summit of Briggs...

138
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:04,660
Captain Buccaneer!!!

139
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:11,620
What was that flash of light from before?

140
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:13,210
There hasn't been a single announcement.

141
00:12:13,710 --> 00:12:17,460
What's going on with military headquarters?

142
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:20,670
No follow-up reports from Radio Capital?

143
00:12:20,670 --> 00:12:22,470
Nope.

144
00:12:22,470 --> 00:12:24,010
What about the other stations?

145
00:12:25,010 --> 00:12:28,350
They're just announcing a curfew for the moment.

146
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:34,270
Mommy!

147
00:12:34,770 --> 00:12:38,060
The radio tells us we can't go outside,

148
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:41,400
so let's hold off on going to Tabasa's house today, okay, Elicia?

149
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,780
What?!

150
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:46,200
We can see the solar eclipse from here, too.

151
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,200
It's about to begin,

152
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:50,790
so let's watch it from here with Mommy.

153
00:13:01,590 --> 00:13:03,090
Izumi!

154
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,220
Where are you?!

155
00:13:06,050 --> 00:13:07,590
Izumi!!

156
00:13:08,590 --> 00:13:11,350
Alex, do you know what just happened?

157
00:13:12,890 --> 00:13:15,850
I heard this from the Elric Brothers in the past.

158
00:13:16,850 --> 00:13:19,020
They said that when they performed human transmutation,

159
00:13:19,020 --> 00:13:22,860
they were dragged into the Gate of Truth by black hands.

160
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,990
What is this "Gate of Truth" you speak of?

161
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:31,080
I have no idea.

162
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:33,290
What did you say?!

163
00:13:33,290 --> 00:13:34,410
Were you able to get in touch with them?

164
00:13:35,710 --> 00:13:38,370
Major General, headquarters is safe.

165
00:13:38,370 --> 00:13:39,460
Good.

166
00:13:39,460 --> 00:13:42,960
And, did you obtain any information pertaining to Miss Izumi's situation?

167
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:46,720
No...

168
00:13:47,220 --> 00:13:48,340
I see...

169
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:50,510
And what else?

170
00:13:52,310 --> 00:13:55,270
During a battle with King Bradley,

171
00:13:55,270 --> 00:14:00,900
Captain Buccaneer, who was defending the main gate,

172
00:14:02,730 --> 00:14:04,400
lost his life along with a few other men.

173
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:09,910
It has been reported that the captain,
working together with someone from Xing,

174
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:14,540
successfully gave Bradley a fatal wound and knocked him down into a canal.

175
00:14:15,870 --> 00:14:17,200
Impossible!

176
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:20,170
There's no way that can be true!

177
00:14:20,170 --> 00:14:24,460
How could that King Bradley die so easily?!

178
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:25,920
He's not human-

179
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:31,140
And what about the main gate?

180
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:33,350
It's still being defended.

181
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:37,140
A homunculus by the name of Greed joined their side,

182
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:39,350
and tore apart the central soldiers at the main gate.

183
00:14:40,020 --> 00:14:41,940
A homunculus?!

184
00:14:42,230 --> 00:14:43,650
Impossible.

185
00:14:43,650 --> 00:14:46,530
A homunculus would never turn its fangs on that man...

186
00:14:47,190 --> 00:14:50,780
Apparently, Captain Buccaneer passed away with a smile.

187
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,280
I see.

188
00:14:56,200 --> 00:15:00,250
If he died with a smile, we can't sit here and weep.

189
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:02,540
Let's proceed!

190
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:03,290
Roger!

191
00:15:04,290 --> 00:15:05,960
Let's go, Mr. Sig.

192
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:09,050
We also need to look for your wife.

193
00:15:10,470 --> 00:15:11,300
Right.

194
00:15:31,110 --> 00:15:32,450
Ouch...

195
00:15:33,070 --> 00:15:33,990
Oww...

196
00:15:34,910 --> 00:15:35,780
Master!

197
00:15:39,250 --> 00:15:40,000
Ed!

198
00:15:40,660 --> 00:15:42,040
Are you okay?!

199
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,870
Yeah, somewhat.

200
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:46,540
What are you doing here?

201
00:15:47,130 --> 00:15:48,920
That's what I want to know.

202
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:51,420
So, where are we?

203
00:15:52,090 --> 00:15:53,800
I don't know.

204
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,680
I was just sent here all of a sudden...

205
00:15:58,310 --> 00:15:59,270
Al!

206
00:16:01,770 --> 00:16:02,230
Al!

207
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:03,140
Hey!

208
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:03,140
Even Al?

209
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:03,690
Get yourself together!

210
00:16:03,690 --> 00:16:06,270
Could it be that all the human sacrifices were gathered?

211
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:05,770
What's wrong, Al?!

212
00:16:06,270 --> 00:16:06,980
Hey!

213
00:16:09,570 --> 00:16:13,070
One, two, three...

214
00:16:15,530 --> 00:16:17,280
...and four.

215
00:16:17,870 --> 00:16:20,290
We're missing one.

216
00:16:23,410 --> 00:16:27,330
I guess the last one is currently being made.

217
00:16:27,630 --> 00:16:31,260
W-What the hell is this monster?

218
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,010
Hohenheim!

219
00:16:34,630 --> 00:16:36,470
Edward...

220
00:16:36,470 --> 00:16:39,430
Even Alphonse was captured...?

221
00:16:39,430 --> 00:16:41,600
Whoa, Miss Izumi as well.

222
00:16:41,850 --> 00:16:45,390
Sorry I'm in such a pitiful state.

223
00:16:45,390 --> 00:16:47,100
What in the world is going on?

224
00:16:47,810 --> 00:16:49,820
Well...

225
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:52,030
You stay put.

226
00:16:52,780 --> 00:16:58,450
I'll slowly absorb the philosopher's stone inside you later.

227
00:16:58,450 --> 00:17:02,040
Who the hell is that dark guy, Hohenheim?!{black guy lol}

228
00:17:02,830 --> 00:17:04,620
My alter ego.

229
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:08,790
The guy who the homunculi called 'Father'.

230
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:14,010
That's the geezer?!

231
00:17:14,550 --> 00:17:16,220
Yeah.

232
00:17:16,220 --> 00:17:18,590
I was able to destroy his skin, but...

233
00:17:19,140 --> 00:17:23,770
Quit your blabbering, Hohenheim.

234
00:17:24,350 --> 00:17:29,980
I welcome you, human sacrifices.

235
00:17:31,230 --> 00:17:34,990
Thanks for coming to my castle.

236
00:17:37,450 --> 00:17:39,070
Al, wake up.

237
00:17:39,070 --> 00:17:41,080
This one's going to be tough.

238
00:17:41,490 --> 00:17:42,540
Al?

239
00:17:43,410 --> 00:17:44,910
Hey, Al!

240
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:46,870
Alphonse!

241
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:53,170
The ones up there are so unreliable.

242
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:58,800
They couldn't even prepare five human sacrifices for this day?

243
00:18:03,390 --> 00:18:08,600
Well, I gathered all the ones who've been seeking morsels like immortality,

244
00:18:08,850 --> 00:18:11,980
so it's no surprise that they couldn't do their jobs.

245
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:19,780
Damn you!

246
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:38,170
Excellent. Stay just like that.

247
00:18:38,970 --> 00:18:43,720
Now, Mustang, we don't have much time.

248
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:46,850
I'd appreciate it if you could willingly cooperate with me.

249
00:18:47,350 --> 00:18:52,270
Do you mind performing human transmutation and opening the gate?

250
00:18:52,270 --> 00:18:53,440
What?

251
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:54,980
I don't care who you transmutate.

252
00:18:56,280 --> 00:19:01,070
Your late parents, your lover, your friend.

253
00:19:01,660 --> 00:19:03,910
The one you were close to...

254
00:19:03,910 --> 00:19:06,040
What was his name again?

255
00:19:06,040 --> 00:19:06,990
Hughes.

256
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:09,750
I don't mind if you transmutate him.

257
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:12,750
We'll take care of all the arrangements.

258
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:16,750
The ones you call... "human sacrifices"?

259
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,460
Precisely.

260
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:22,050
Those who open the gate can become human sacrifices.

261
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:25,760
So that's why the Elric Brothers were chosen.

262
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:27,220
Yup.

263
00:19:27,680 --> 00:19:31,520
I heard from them that human transmutation doesn't work.

264
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:34,610
What idiot would try it when they know it's not going to work?!

265
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:37,360
Good point there.

266
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:40,740
So as long as you open the gate and come back, it's fine.

267
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:42,820
I refuse!

268
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:44,700
I won't perform human transmutation!

269
00:19:44,700 --> 00:19:45,950
I won't open the gate either!

270
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:55,210
Didn't I tell you that we don't have much time?

271
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:03,760
Lieutenant!

272
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,430
Lieutenant?!

273
00:20:05,430 --> 00:20:06,350
Lieutenant!

274
00:20:07,010 --> 00:20:11,930
Now, open the gate, Mustang.

275
00:20:11,930 --> 00:20:13,600
You scum!!

276
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:17,440
Lieutenant! Can you hear me?!

277
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:18,730
Say something!

278
00:20:19,110 --> 00:20:23,570
Now, perform human transmutation and become the fifth sacrifice.

279
00:20:26,370 --> 00:20:31,040
Come on, if you don't pick up the pace, this woman will die.

280
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,710
Oh, I get it.

281
00:20:33,710 --> 00:20:36,960
You're going to transmute her back after she dies?

282
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,840
That's fine too.

283
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,300
I won't die...

284
00:20:44,550 --> 00:20:49,680
I've been ordered not to die...

285
00:20:50,310 --> 00:20:53,730
If one could obtain an immortal body with an order like that,

286
00:20:53,730 --> 00:20:56,230
everyone would live without worry.

287
00:20:56,980 --> 00:21:00,610
What will you do, Mustang?

288
00:21:00,610 --> 00:21:04,030
A woman who's precious to you is dying.

289
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,780
If you leave her be, she'll die from blood loss.

290
00:21:08,530 --> 00:21:12,830
But I'm a doctor well-versed in alchemy,

291
00:21:12,830 --> 00:21:16,210
and tadaa, I even have a philosopher's stone.

292
00:21:16,750 --> 00:21:25,130
In other words, I can save this woman's life.

293
00:21:27,090 --> 00:21:34,430
Well, if she dies before you make a decision, there'll be nothing I can do.

294
00:21:35,980 --> 00:21:37,020
Oh?

295
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:43,650
She's gotten quiet.

296
00:21:43,650 --> 00:21:45,690
I wonder if she died.

297
00:21:47,450 --> 00:21:48,450
Colonel...

298
00:21:49,910 --> 00:21:55,620
There's no need... for you to perform human transmutation.

299
00:21:56,540 --> 00:21:59,420
You'll do it, won't you, Mustang?

300
00:22:10,470 --> 00:22:11,970
Now!

301
00:22:23,650 --> 00:22:25,070
I will.

302
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:42,800
Ever since that day passed,

303
00:22:39,250 --> 00:22:42,800
Ano hi kara zutto

304
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:47,050
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

305
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:47,050
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

306
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:52,600
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

307
00:22:47,590 --> 00:22:52,600
Itami wo kasanetemo

308
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,710
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

309
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:57,710
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

310
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,150
I'll never be able

311
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:01,150
Mou modorenai

312
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,650
to return to those days.

313
00:23:01,150 --> 00:23:03,650
Ikutsumo no hibi

314
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:08,740
I'm still powerless.

315
00:23:03,650 --> 00:23:08,740
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

316
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,990
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

317
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,990
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

318
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:19,860
memories of when you were still with me.

319
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:19,860
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

320
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,880
I long to become

321
00:23:20,540 --> 00:23:22,880
Kyou yori motto

322
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,630
stronger than I am now,

323
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:25,630
Tsuyoku naritai

324
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:30,770
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

325
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:30,770
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

326
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,140
If the wind happens to stop

327
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:33,140
Arukitsuzukete

328
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:35,850
in the midst of my long journey,

329
00:23:33,140 --> 00:23:35,850
Kaze ga yandara

330
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:40,560
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

331
00:23:35,850 --> 00:23:40,560
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

332
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:47,900
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

333
00:23:41,310 --> 00:23:47,900
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

334
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:53,450
A rainbow spans across the sky.

335
00:23:49,070 --> 00:23:53,450
Niji ga kakaruyo

336
00:23:58,990 --> 00:24:02,960
Though there may be favorable turn,

337
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:06,540
know that this repose last but a moment.

338
00:24:07,290 --> 00:24:12,130
The place upon which thou standest is the entrance to the netherworld.

339
00:24:13,510 --> 00:24:17,640
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

340
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:22,140
Episode 59, Lost Light.

341
00:24:17,660 --> 00:24:22,160
Lost Light

342
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:27,110
The end is near.
